### Filter on "-to-one" relations

Prisma Client provides the [`is`](/orm/v7/reference/prisma-client-reference#is) and [`isNot`](/orm/v7/reference/prisma-client-reference#isnot) options to filter records by the properties of related records on the "-to-one" side of the relation. For example, filtering posts based on properties of their author.

For example, the following query returns `Post` records that meet the following criteria:

- Author's name is not Bob
- Author is older than 40

```ts
const users = await prisma.post.findMany({
  where: {
    author: {
      // [!code highlight]
      isNot: {
        // [!code highlight]
        name: "Bob", // [!code highlight]
      }, // [!code highlight]
      is: {
        // [!code highlight]
        age: {
          // [!code highlight]
          gt: 40, // [!code highlight]
        }, // [!code highlight]
      }, // [!code highlight]
    }, // [!code highlight]
  }, // [!code highlight]
  include: {
    author: true,
  },
});
```

